From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 16:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: amvx: report the real VP8 decode frame-size limit

mvx_session_enum_framesizes() grouped MVX_FORMAT_VP8 with H.263 and
MPEG-4 and so reported a maximum of 2048x2048 for VP8. That is not what
the hardware does.

Measured on Sky1 (Linlon MVE v8), VP8 decode is bit-exact against libvpx
at 2048x1152, 3840x2160, 4096x2304 and 4096x4096, and fails at 5120x2880
with "capture buffer initialization (Input/output error)". The real
decode limit is 4096x4096.

The under-report is not cosmetic. V4L2 clients that honour
VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES refuse to use the hardware above the advertised
size, so Chromium fell back to software for 4K VP8 while ffmpeg - which
does not consult the enumeration - decoded the same stream on the VPU
bit-exact. With this change Chromium decodes 3840x2160 VP8 on the VPU.

Encode keeps the conservative 2048x2048; it was not measured.

Upstream-Status: Pending (to be sent to CIX)
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/if/mvx_session.c
+++ b/driver/if/mvx_session.c
@@ -6827,10 +6827,34 @@
         break;
     case MVX_FORMAT_H263:
     case MVX_FORMAT_MPEG4:
-    case MVX_FORMAT_VP8:
         *max_width = 2048;
         *max_height = 2048;
         break;
+    case MVX_FORMAT_VP8:
+        /*
+         * VP8 decode was reported as 2048x2048 only because it shared a case
+         * with H.263 and MPEG-4. Measured on Sky1 (Linlon MVE v8), VP8 decode
+         * is bit-exact against libvpx at 2048x1152, 3840x2160, 4096x2304 and
+         * 4096x4096, and fails at 5120x2880 with
+         * "capture buffer initialization (Input/output error)". The real
+         * decode limit is 4096x4096.
+         *
+         * This matters because V4L2 clients that honour
+         * VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES refuse the hardware above the reported size:
+         * Chromium fell back to software for 4K VP8, while ffmpeg - which
+         * does not consult the enumeration - decoded the same stream on the
+         * VPU bit-exact.
+         *
+         * Encode keeps the conservative 2048x2048; it was not measured.
+         */
+        if (is_encoder) {
+            *max_width = 2048;
+            *max_height = 2048;
+        } else {
+            *max_width = 4096;
+            *max_height = 4096;
+        }
+        break;
     case MVX_FORMAT_JPEG:
         if (is_encoder) {
             *max_width = 16384;
